# Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in. Sourced by every Slurm job and by
# slurm/chain.sh on the login node.

# Slurm account, if your Unity login has more than one or no default.
# SLURM_ACCOUNT=pi_someone_umass_edu

# Where ~45GB of model weights go. Never a home directory: Unity's home quota
# is far smaller than that. /work/pi_<account>/<user> or /scratch/workspace/<user>.
# HF_HOME=/work/pi_someone_umass_edu/$USER/hf_cache

# Gated or private checkpoints only; Qwen2.5 needs no token.
# HF_TOKEN=hf_...

# Results root (default: results/unity in the repo).
# CARRIERS_RESULTS=/work/pi_someone_umass_edu/$USER/carriers-results

# Models. Open weights, served locally by vLLM: this project uses no OpenAI or
# Anthropic key anywhere, for the agents or for the judge. The judge is
# deliberately larger than the agents.
#
#   agents   Qwen/Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct      default; ungated, one A100-40GB
#            Qwen/Qwen2.5-14B-Instruct     stronger agents, ~2x the GPU-hours
#            meta-llama/Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct   gated: accept the license, set HF_TOKEN
#   judge    Qwen/Qwen2.5-14B-Instruct     default; ungated, fits one A100-40GB
#            Qwen/Qwen2.5-32B-Instruct-AWQ  bigger judge, still one 40GB card
#            meta-llama/Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct   judge from another family, as a
#                                           robustness check on the judge delta
#
# The tool-call parser follows the family automatically (hermes / llama3_json);
# override it, and Llama's tool chat template, only if you change that mapping.
# AGENT_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct
# JUDGE_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen2.5-14B-Instruct
# TOOL_CALL_PARSER=hermes
# VLLM_CHAT_TEMPLATE=/path/to/tool_chat_template_llama3.1_json.jinja

# Override any #SBATCH directive without editing the scripts: sbatch reads these.
# SBATCH_PARTITION=gpu-preempt
# SBATCH_CONSTRAINT=a100|vram40
